## Q3 (gui-stack-v1-issues) — a `do … end` block passed to a FREE function
## with an explicit closure parameter. Before the fix this compiled but
## segfaulted: a block-bearing free call was lowered as `runit.call(block)`
## (treating the function as a closure value) instead of forwarding the block
## as `runit`'s argument. Covers no-arg, plain `Fn`, and a block with params.

def runit(f: any Fn[Fn() -> nil]) -> nil
  f.()
end

def withn(f: any Fn[Fn(Int) -> nil]) -> nil
  f.(7)
end

def plain(f: Fn() -> nil) -> nil
  f.()
end

def main
  runit do
    puts "plain-any"
  end
  withn do |n|
    puts "n=#{n}"
  end
  plain do
    puts "plain-fn"
  end
end
